877:Keys are `http_cache_<sha256 of the request URL>` for the body and `http_cache_timestamp_<body key>` for the write time, plus `http_cache_index`, a `StringList` of every body key currently written. The URL is hashed, query included, so a token in a query string is never written to disk as a key or in the index. Entries an earlier version stored under the verbatim URL, and listed in `http_cache_index`, are removed the first time any request passes through, whether `CacheConfig.enableCache` is on or off; an entry written before the index existed cannot be found and stays until the app's data is cleared.
